HV049,"📝The precedent is sad📝 what will happen to the oil going to Cuba?  Although the Americans have given concessions for Russian oil, this has little to do with Cuba. One of the tankers, which was heading to Cuba, has already changed direction, and the other, Anatoly Kolodkin, is still moving across the Atlantic Ocean.  🖍Against the backdrop of ongoing arrests and detentions of cargo ships flying the Russian or third flag, security for the entire Russian merchant fleet is a very ephemeral concept in our time.  🚩Currently there is still an amphibious landing group off the coast of Cuba, as well as one cruiser. This does not include frigates or, as they are called, littoral combat ships of the US Navy. And if necessary, they can seize any ship.  🏳️And if no agreements were reached regarding the Russian tanker on passage to Cuba, then the question will arise: what if the United States decides to seize this Russian ship on the basis of the blockade of Cuba?  ❗️In a situation where the protection of shipping is based on dying global legislation, it is time to think about how to ensure the protection of your assets, of which there are not so many, given all the attacks and detentions. And there’s no need to talk about image costs. #Cuba #Russia 🔪 [USER] - the pulse of the New World 💸Support us",,,,,,
