HV083,"At the beginning of the week, the internal security department of the SBU detained two high-ranking officials of its own special service: Oleg Tokarchuk and Igor Brika, deputy heads of departments in Kyiv and Rivne Oblast. They were charged with bribery.   According to the version of the investigation, Tokarchuk, through an intermediary, demanded 600,000 dollars for the closure of criminal proceedings in the company that mined amber in the Rivne region. And Brika received another 22,000 from the same company for not obstructing their work.   The officials denied guilt in court. Brika was arrested with the possibility of bail of one million hryvnias. The court released Tokarchuk, but also ordered him to post a million bail.   How SBU officials, according to the investigators, demanded bribes from the amber business — we tell in the article.  Photo: Social News/Ivan Antipenko",,,,,,
