HV211,"📝Iranian War📝 main events leading up to the outcome of March 22 On the twenty-third day of the war, the coalition continued attacks on Iran, and the Iranians continued missile attacks on Israel. At the same time, pressure is increasing on the Strait of Hormuz, energy and logistics in the region.  ➡️In Iran, strikes occurred in Tehran, Bushehr and Bandar Abbas. Despite the intense attacks, air defenses continue to operate, and claims of interceptions and downed targets indicate that some capabilities are retained.   ➡️Israel has again recorded arrivals after attacks on Dimona and Arad. Against this background, an internal reaction also manifests itself. During a visit by officials to the stricken city, National Security Minister Itamar Ben-Gvir faced harsh criticism from local residents.   ➡️In the Lebanese-Israeli direction, Hezbollah struck the Misgav-Ama area. The Israelis hold positions in At-Taiba, but the front line remains stable and shelling from both sides continues.   ➡️A new incident was recorded near Sharjah in the Persian Gulf - an explosion occurred next to a commercial ship without a direct hit.   ➡️The United States has started talking about possible negotiations, but the conditions involve Iran abandoning its missile and nuclear programs and effectively limiting its regional activity. At the same time, Donald Trump is threatening attacks on energy infrastructure.   ➡️In parallel, the war is already hitting the United States itself. The current campaign is rapidly depleting stocks of precision-guided weapons and air defense missiles. At the same time, the pace of production does not cover the costs, and the attempt to simultaneously support several directions calls into question the very concept of “two theaters of war.”  ➡️In Iraq, the exchange of blows between American forces and pro-Iranian groups continues. At the same time, the situation in the oil and gas sector is deteriorating - foreign companies are suspending work and evacuating staff.   ➡️In Syria in Al-Qamishli, Kurdish formations captured the security headquarters during the celebration of Nowruz and replaced the state flags. Retaliatory actions by regime supporters and tribal groups show growing tensions in the country.   ➡️Against the background of the crisis, payments in yuan for passage through the Strait of Hormuz are being discussed. However, in Japan and China such schemes are assessed with caution due to risks to the financial system and a possible reaction from the United States.   📎High-resolution maps: 🔸Hot spots of instability (ru; en) 🔸Strikes on Iran (ru; en) 🔸Strikes on Israel (ru; en) 🔸Strikes on Lebanon (ru; en) 🔸Strikes on Iraq (ru; en) 🔸Situation in the Strait of Hormuz (ru; en) #Iran #digest #Israel #Iraq #map #Lebanon #Syria #USA #UAE ✈ RU | ✈ EN | ✉ MAX ✉ VK | ✉ RuTube | ✉ OK | ✉Zen 💸Support us",,,,,,
