HV219,"Iran and Hezbollah have carried out an extensive and sustained campaign of strikes against ""Israel"", according to the Israeli Alma Research Center’s latest report. Since the start of the war, Iran has launched at least 329 attack waves, maintaining an average pace of around 11 strikes per day, with the ability to surge intensity during peak periods and expand its focus from central ""Israel"" toward the south.  At the same time, Hezbollah’s involvement has been even more numerically significant. Since joining the war on March 2, the group has carried out 779 attack waves, with activity steadily increasing after initial fluctuations and reaching higher, more consistent levels in recent days, said the report.  The report highlights a sharp escalation over the March 20–21 weekend alone, when 110 Hezbollah attack waves were recorded in just two days.",,,,,,
