HV261,"After nearly 28 months of tireless efforts, and as this page now ceases its 24/7 activity, we want to say thank you, from the deepest place in our heart.  To every person who stood by the families, who refused to look away, who stayed. Everyone who took part in this fight to bring the hostages home became part of history, the largest civil movement in Israel since 1948.  You echoed the families’ pain, their cries, and even their rare moments of joy. You embraced the hostages and their families as if we were your family, too. You carried them when they could not carry themselves.  Your likes. Your comments. Your follows. Your shares.  They were never small gestures. Know this: they were a lifeline. They were a wave of human compassion that pierced through the darkest nightmare.  They were threads in a monumental force that moved mountains, touched every corner of the earth, and brought our loved ones home.  One day, when people ask, ‘Where were you during this time?’ You’ll be able to say: I was there. I did not stay silent. I was part of Bring Them Home Now. I helped bring them home.  Thank you for carrying us. Thank you for never giving up. Thank you for bringing them home 💛  Bring Them Home Now by [USER] A [USER] project - Other backups: [USER]",,,,,,
